<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 July, from 356 BCE to 1969.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/herostratus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/herostratus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/356-bce">356 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Herostratus burns the Temple of Artemis at Ephesus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herostratus">Herostratus</a> set fire to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-artemis">Temple of Artemis at Ephesus</a>, one of the Seven Wonders of the ancient world. The 6th-century BCE marble temple, partly paid for by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus of Lydia</a>, was rebuilt on an even larger scale.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/temple-of-artemis">Temple of Artemis</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/356-bce">356 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,381 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander the Great is born in Pella</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alexander, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a>, was born by the traditional dating around 20 or 21 July. By his death at 32 he had conquered an empire stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to north-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/905">905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Berengar I has his rival Emperor Louis III blinded</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Louis III, emperor and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, captured at Verona by his rival Berengar I, was blinded for breaking his oath and forced to give up both crowns. Remembered as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-blind">Louis the Blind</a>, he returned to rule Provence.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-blind">Louis the Blind</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berengar-i-of-italy">Berengar I of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1242">1242 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">784 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis IX defeats Henry III of England at Taillebourg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charente">Charente</a> at Taillebourg, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a> and his stepfather Hugh X of Lusignan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saintonge-war">Saintonge War</a>'s decisive battle. The failure ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s attempt to recover Poitou.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-taillebourg">Battle of Taillebourg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-ix-of-france">Louis IX of France</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-of-england">Henry III of England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1588">1588 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">438 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">English ships first engage the Spanish Armada off Plymouth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The English fleet under Lord Howard and Drake attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Armada</a> off Plymouth (21 July Old Style). The running fight up the Channel ended at Gravelines and in the Armada's disastrous voyage home.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1773">1773 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Clement XIV suppresses the Jesuits</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Under pressure from the Catholic monarchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and Portugal, Clement XIV dissolved the Society of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a>. The order survived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and was restored worldwide in 1814.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1798">1798 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">228 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon defeats the Mamluks at the Battle of the Pyramids</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French infantry squares broke the charges of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> cavalry near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. The victory gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where his expedition's scholars laid the foundations of modern Egyptology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1925">1925 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">101 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Scopes is found guilty of teaching evolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Dayton jury convicted teacher John Scopes of breaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a>'s ban on teaching human evolution, and he was fined 100 dollars. The verdict was later overturned on a technicality.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1969">1969 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">57 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Armstrong and Aldrin lift off from the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After about 21 hours on the lunar surface, Armstrong and Aldrin fired the ascent stage of Eagle to rejoin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michael-collins">Michael Collins</a> in lunar orbit. They left a plaque reading 'We came in peace for all mankind'.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 July <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wen-of-sui"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-wen-of-sui.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Wen of Sui</span><span class="tp">541–604</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-sixtus-iv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-sixtus-iv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Sixtus IV</span><span class="tp">1414–1484</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-julius-reuter"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-julius-reuter.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul Julius Reuter</span><span class="tp">1816–1899</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/milan-rastislav-stefanik"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/milan-rastislav-stefanik.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Milan Rastislav Štefánik</span><span class="tp">1880–1919</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marshall-mcluhan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marshall-mcluhan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marshall McLuhan</span><span class="tp">1911–1980</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 July <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kan-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kan-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">K'an II</span><span class="tp">588–658</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-palaiologos"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/manuel-ii-palaiologos.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Manuel II Palaiologos</span><span class="tp">1350–1425</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-mendoza"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antonio-de-mendoza.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antonio de Mendoza</span><span class="tp">1495–1552</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-butler-1st-duke-of-ormonde"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-butler-1st-duke-of-ormonde.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Butler, 1st Duke of Ormonde</span><span class="tp">1610–1688</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/claus-von-stauffenberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Claus von Stauffenberg</span><span class="tp">1907–1944</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jigme-dorji-wangchuck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jigme-dorji-wangchuck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jigme Dorji Wangchuck</span><span class="tp">1929–1972</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
